{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeRotation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeRotation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeWedgePair"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_wedgeAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_wedgeAt","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L228-L240","doc":"**The hyperbolic volume of the chimney over a wedge at any axis is `Λ(ψ)`.**\n\nH4-5b's value, freed from the positive `x`-axis.  This is what an assembly of\nthree wedges at three different axes would consume.\n\n**Still not a statement about an ideal tetrahedron**, and H4-5c is still open:\nwhat remains is showing that a triangle inscribed in the circle *is* the union\nof three such wedges up to null sets. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.lintegral_wedgeAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.lintegral_wedgeAt","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L218-L226","doc":"**The base integral over a wedge at ANY axis is `Λ(ψ)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.baseIntegrand_rotL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.baseIntegrand_rotL","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L209-L216","doc":"The base integrand is rotation-invariant: it sees the point only through\n`x² + y²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_subset_disk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_subset_disk","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L197-L205","doc":"The rotated wedge still lies strictly inside the disk — rotation fixes\n`x² + y²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_wedgeAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_wedgeAt","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L193-L195","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_eq_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_eq_image","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L172-L191","doc":"**The rotated-frame wedge IS the rotated wedge** — the theorem the\nCartesian definition exists in order to make provable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inner_v_rotL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inner_v_rotL","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L165-L170","doc":"…and projecting on the perpendicular returns the ordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inner_u_rotL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.inner_u_rotL","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L158-L163","doc":"Rotating by `θ`, then projecting on the `θ`-axis, returns the abscissa. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L147-L156","doc":"**The wedge with axis direction `θ`** — the open isoceles triangle with\napex at the circumcentre, apex angle `2ψ`, and its axis of symmetry pointing\nin direction `θ`.\n\nCut out by dot products against the rotated frame `u = (cos θ, sin θ)`,\n`v = (−sin θ, cos θ)`, so that `wedgeAt R 0 ψ` is `wedge R ψ` on the nose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.lintegral_rotL_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.lintegral_rotL_image","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L127-L141","doc":"**Rotation invariance of the base integral.**\n\nThe hypothesis `hg` is where the integrand's own rotation-invariance is\nrequired; measure-preservation alone would not suffice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotL_normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotL_normSq","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L120-L125","doc":"Rotation preserves the squared distance to the origin. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurePreserving_rotE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurePreserving_rotE","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L101-L111","doc":"**Rotation preserves Lebesgue measure on the plane.**\n\nVia `det = 1`: not via an isometry, because `ℝ × ℝ` does not carry the\nEuclidean norm (see the file header). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotE_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotE_injective","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L98-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotE_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotE_apply","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotE","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L82-L94","doc":"**Rotation as a measurable equivalence**, with `rot (−θ)` as inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotL_neg_rotL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotL_neg_rotL","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L74-L80","doc":"Rotating by `θ` and then by `−θ` is the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.det_rotL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.det_rotL","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L67-L72","doc":"**`det(rot θ) = 1`** — the Pythagorean identity, and the only fact about\nrotation that Lebesgue measure cares about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotL_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotL_apply","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L63-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.rotL","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeRotation.lean#L57-L61","doc":"**Rotation of the plane by `θ`**, as an `ℝ`-linear map. ","signatureChunk":0}]}